From: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:12:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-119265: Memory corruption in Quota

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8620633:
Remove obsolete QuotaDatabase::MoveLegacyDatabase()

QuotaDatabase::MoveLegacyDatabase() was added in April 2022 (M103,
https://crrev.com/c/3513545) to copy <profile>/QuotaManager and its
journal into <profile>/WebStorage/. Because it used base::PathExists()
and base::CopyFile() without checking for symbolic links (and did not
check whether the destination journal path already existed), a symlink
at <profile>/WebStorage/QuotaManager-journal would be followed when
EnsureOpened() or RecoverOrRaze() ran in the browser process.

Prior to M103, QuotaDatabase was at schema version 8, and support for
all schema versions < 10 has already been removed in
QuotaDatabaseMigrations::UpgradeSchema() (https://crrev.com/c/6990378),
meaning any pre-M103 database would immediately fail
EnsureDatabaseVersion() and be razed by ResetStorage() anyway.

Remove MoveLegacyDatabase(), legacy_db_file_path_, and the obsolete
migration tests, and add a regression test verifying that legacy files
in the profile root are ignored and symlinks in WebStorage are not
followed.

